  "changes_data": [
    {
      "diff": "@@ -14,7 +14,7 @@ It is used for troubleshooting, analysis, development and education.\n \n == What’s New\n \n-__We no longer ship official 32-bit Windows packages starting with this release__.\n+__We do not ship official 32-bit Windows packages for Wireshark 4.0 and later__.\n If you need to use Wireshark on that platform, we recommend using the latest 3.6 release.\n wsbuglink:17779[]\n \n@@ -42,7 +42,21 @@ The following bugs have been fixed:\n //* cveidlink:2014-2486[]\n //* Wireshark insists on subscribing to two dozen streaming services but only watches three.\n \n-* wsbuglink:18413[No Audio in RTP player with Wireshark 4.0.0] - RTP player do not play audio frequently on Win32 builds with Qt6\n+* Comparing a boolean field against 1 always succeeds on big-endian machines. wsbuglink:12236[].\n+* Qt: MaxMind GeoIP columns not added to Endpoints table. wsbuglink:18320[].\n+* Fuzz job crash output: fuzz-2022-10-04-7131.pcap. wsbuglink:18402[].\n+* The RTP player might not play audio on Windows. wsbuglink:18413[].\n+* Wireshark 4.0 breaks display filter expression with > sign. wsbuglink:18418[].\n+* Capture filters not working when using SSH capture and dumpcap. wsbuglink:18420[].\n+* Packet diagram field values are not terminated. wsbuglink:18428[].\n+* Packet bytes not displayed completely if scrolling. wsbuglink:18438[].\n+* Fuzz job crash output: fuzz-2022-10-13-7166.pcap. wsbuglink:18467[].\n+* Decoding bug H.245 userInput Signal. wsbuglink:18468[].\n+* CFDP dissector doesn't handle \\\"destination filename\\\" only. wsbuglink:18495[].\n+* Home page capture button doesn't pop up capture options dialog. wsbuglink:18506[].\n+* Missing dot in H.248 protocol name. wsbuglink:18513[].\n+* Missing dot for protocol H.264 in protocol column. wsbuglink:18524[].\n+* Fuzz job crash output: fuzz-2022-10-23-7240.pcap. wsbuglink:18534[].\n \n === New and Updated Features\n \n@@ -69,18 +83,39 @@ There are no new protocols in this release.\n === Updated Protocol Support\n \n // Add one protocol per line between the -- delimiters.\n-// ag -A1 '(define PSNAME|proto_register_protocol[^_])' $(git diff --name-only v4.0.0.. | ag packet- | sort -u)\n+// ag -A1 '(define PSNAME|proto_register_protocol[^_])' $(git diff --name-only v4.0.1.. | ag packet- | sort -u)\n [commaize]\n --\n+ASN.1 PER\n+CFDP\n+Diameter\n+DirectPlay\n+F5 Ethernet Trailer\n+GTP\n+H.223\n+H.248\n+H.264\n+H.265\n+IEEE 802.11\n+IPv4\n+MBIM\n+O-RAN FH CUS\n+PFCP\n+RTCP\n+SCTP\n+SMB\n+TCP\n+TRANSUM\n --\n \n === New and Updated Capture File Support\n \n-There is no new or updated capture file support in this release.\n+// There is no new or updated capture file support in this release.\n // Add one file type per line between the -- delimiters.\n-// [commaize]\n-// --\n-// --\n+[commaize]\n+--\n+BLF\n+--\n \n // === New and Updated Capture Interfaces support\n \n",
